<% content_for :title, "On Mixed Episodes | Bipolar Sober" %>

<style>
  .mixed-page {
    background: #080808;
    color: #fff;
    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
  }

  .mixed-page *,
  .mixed-page *::before,
  .mixed-page *::after {
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  .mixed-hero {
    min-height: 85vh;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 80px 6%;
    background-color: #080808;
    background-image:
      linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(8, 8, 8, .55), transparent),
      url("<%= asset_path('bipolar_mixed_episodes_desktop.png') %>");
    background-size: cover;
    background-position: center;
  }

  .mixed-hero-content {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .mixed-eyebrow {
    max-width: 440px;
    margin: 0 0 28px;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.6;
    letter-spacing: .12em;
  }

  .mixed-hero h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(56px, 8vw, 120px);
    font-weight: 900;
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: .9;
    letter-spacing: -.055em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .mixed-hero h1 span {
    display: block;
  }

  .mixed-intro {
    margin: 32px 0 0;
    font-size: clamp(15px, 1.6vw, 22px);
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .mixed-quote {
    padding: 48px 6%;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .mixed-quote blockquote {
    max-width: 1000px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .mixed-quote blockquote p {
    margin: 0 0 20px;
    color: #eaff00;
    font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 56px);
    font-weight: 900;
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .mixed-quote cite {
    font-size: 14px;
    font-style: normal;
  }

  .mixed-section {
    padding: 72px 6%;
  }

  .mixed-section-inner {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, .85fr) minmax(0, 1.15fr);
    gap: 60px;
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .mixed-number {
    margin: 0 0 22px;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: .12em;
  }

  .mixed-section h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(36px, 4.5vw, 68px);
    font-weight: 900;
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: .95;
    letter-spacing: -.045em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .mixed-copy {
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .mixed-copy p {
    margin: 0 0 22px;
  }

  .mixed-copy p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .mixed-copy ul {
    margin: 0 0 24px;
    padding-left: 22px;
  }

  .mixed-copy li {
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .mixed-pink {
    background: #ff1493;
    color: #080808;
  }

  .mixed-yellow {
    background: #eaff00;
    color: #080808;
  }

  .mixed-purple {
    background: #8a00ff;
    color: #fff;
  }

  .mixed-black {
    background: #080808;
    color: #fff;
  }

  .mixed-white {
    background: #fff;
    color: #080808;
  }

  .mixed-takeaway {
    padding-top: 22px;
    border-top: 3px solid currentColor;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .mixed-footer {
    padding: 40px 6%;
    border-top: 1px solid #444;
  }

  .mixed-footer-inner {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 24px;
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .mixed-footer a {
    color: #eaff00;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.5;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .mixed-footer a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .mixed-footer a:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid #ff1493;
    outline-offset: 6px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .mixed-hero {
      min-height: 88svh;
      align-items: flex-start;
      padding: 48px 6% 60px;
      background-image:
        url("<%= asset_path('bipolar_mixed_episodes_mobile.png') %>");
      background-position: center bottom;
    }

    .mixed-eyebrow {
      margin-bottom: 24px;
      font-size: 10px;
    }

    .mixed-hero h1 {
      font-size: clamp(44px, 13.5vw, 94px);
    }

    .mixed-intro {
      margin-top: 24px;
      font-size: 14px;
    }

    .mixed-section {
      padding: 48px 6%;
    }

    .mixed-section-inner {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 28px;
    }

    .mixed-section h2 {
      font-size: clamp(36px, 10vw, 58px);
    }

    .mixed-copy {
      font-size: 16px;
      line-height: 1.8;
    }

    .mixed-number {
      margin-bottom: 16px;
    }
  }
</style>

<main class="mixed-page">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="mixed-hero" aria-labelledby="mixed-title">
    <div class="mixed-hero-content">

      <p class="mixed-eyebrow">
        BIPOLAR SOBER / BIPOLAR / MIXED EPISODES
      </p>

      <h1 id="mixed-title">
        <span>ON MIXED</span>
        <span>EPISODES.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="mixed-intro">
        EXHAUSTED AND WIRED.<br>
        MISERABLE AND RESTLESS.<br>
        AN ENGINE THAT WON’T TURN OFF.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- QUOTE -->
  <section class="mixed-quote" aria-label="Opening quote">
    <blockquote>
      <p>“We’re all mad here.”</p>
      <cite>— The Cheshire Cat</cite>
    </blockquote>
  </section>


  <!-- 01 / THE CONTRADICTIONS -->
  <section class="mixed-section mixed-purple">
    <div class="mixed-section-inner">

      <div class="mixed-section-heading">
        <p class="mixed-number">01 / WIRED AND MISERABLE</p>

        <h2>
          TIRED AS<br>
          FUCK.<br>
          STILL<br>
          RUNNING.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="mixed-copy">
        <p>
          You feel like shit, but your brain will not shut the
          fuck up. You want to withdraw, yet sitting still feels
          unbearable. Your thoughts move quickly and keep taking
          you somewhere painful.
        </p>

        <p>
          Mixed experiences can bring urgency without optimism
          and activity without enjoyment. You want something
          to change immediately without knowing what would help.
        </p>

        <p class="mixed-takeaway">
          Describe what you can observe. You do not have to make
          the contradictions fit a neat category before asking
          your treatment team for help.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 02 / ACCEPTANCE -->
  <section class="mixed-section mixed-yellow">
    <div class="mixed-section-inner">

      <div class="mixed-section-heading">
        <p class="mixed-number">02 / ACKNOWLEDGE WHAT’S HERE</p>

        <h2>
          BOTH CAN<br>
          BE TRUE.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="mixed-copy">
        <p>
          You can feel exhausted and restless. Want company and
          find conversation overwhelming. Need help and feel
          irritated about needing it.
        </p>

        <p>
          “I should relax.” “I should get something done.”
          “I should know what the fuck I want.”
          Those demands add frustration to an already difficult
          experience. Acknowledge what is happening before
          demanding a different state.
        </p>

        <p>
          Try “This is extremely uncomfortable, and I need support
          getting through it.” You do not have to convince yourself
          everything is fine. Choose words that leave room for help.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 03 / IMPULSIVITY -->
  <section class="mixed-section mixed-pink">
    <div class="mixed-section-inner">

      <div class="mixed-section-heading">
        <p class="mixed-number">03 / URGENCY ISN’T AN INSTRUCTION</p>

        <h2>
          DON’T REDO<br>
          YOUR LIFE<br>
          TONIGHT.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="mixed-copy">
        <p>
          Spending, a new project, or an abrupt decision can
          promise relief. Ask what you expect it to accomplish.
          Will it address a need or leave another problem
          once the immediate satisfaction wears off?
        </p>

        <p>
          Make the next decision smaller. Postpone the purchase,
          leave the message unsent, and write down the idea
          without committing. Ask someone you trust to help
          review decisions that feel urgent.
        </p>

        <p class="mixed-takeaway">
          Treat the pause as a practical challenge: what would
          protect you through the next stretch and leave fewer
          consequences afterward?
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 04 / REDUCE DEMANDS -->
  <section class="mixed-section mixed-black">
    <div class="mixed-section-inner">

      <div class="mixed-section-heading">
        <p class="mixed-number">04 / TURN DOWN THE INPUT</p>

        <h2>
          FEWER TABS.<br>
          LESS NOISE.<br>
          ONE STEP.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="mixed-copy">
        <p>
          Close extra tabs, silence unnecessary notifications,
          and choose something familiar and undemanding.
          Give yourself fewer things to respond to.
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>Feel your feet against the floor or name five things you can see.</li>
          <li>Breathe gently, slowing your exhale if that feels comfortable.</li>
          <li>Eat something simple, drink water, and protect your usual sleep routine.</li>
          <li>Leave nonessential tasks unfinished and reduce demands on your time.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          Avoid pushing through exhaustion with caffeine or
          trying to escape agitation with alcohol or weed.
          You do not have to become perfectly calm or wear
          yourself out to earn rest.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 05 / SUPPORT -->
  <section class="mixed-section mixed-white">
    <div class="mixed-section-inner">

      <div class="mixed-section-heading">
        <p class="mixed-number">05 / SAY WHAT’S HAPPENING</p>

        <h2>
          GIVE HELP<br>
          SOMETHING<br>
          TO WORK<br>
          WITH.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="mixed-copy">
        <p>
          “I feel depressed, but my thoughts are racing and
          I’m getting impulsive” tells someone more than
          “I’m having a bad day.” Contact your treatment team
          and describe the experience as accurately as you can.
        </p>

        <p>
          Make a specific request: check in tonight, help you
          stay off shopping sites, or sit with you while you
          contact your psych. When reflection feels beyond
          reach, rely more on prepared safeguards and support.
        </p>

        <p>
          Notice the parts that want to escape, act, criticize,
          or protect you. Listen with curiosity while choosing
          actions that support your safety and stability.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 06 / AFTERWARD -->
  <section class="mixed-section mixed-yellow">
    <div class="mixed-section-inner">

      <div class="mixed-section-heading">
        <p class="mixed-number">06 / PROTECT THE NEXT STEP</p>

        <h2>
          ROOM TO<br>
          BREATHE.<br>
          THEN<br>
          UNDERSTAND.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="mixed-copy">
        <p>
          Afterward, the experience may be difficult to explain.
          You were doing things but felt awful. You wanted relief
          and made decisions that complicated your life.
          Address the consequences specifically and discuss
          what support could enter earlier next time.
        </p>

        <p>
          You do not have to make the episode meaningful while
          getting through it. Eating, postponing a purchase,
          settling somewhere quieter, or asking for help can
          each be a useful next step.
        </p>

        <p class="mixed-takeaway">
          You deserve care when your feelings contradict each
          other and your usual coping skills feel insufficient.
          Let the next step protect you. Understanding can come later.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- NAVIGATION -->
  <nav class="mixed-footer" aria-label="Bipolar topic navigation">
    <div class="mixed-footer-inner">
      <%= link_to "← BACK TO BIPOLAR", bipolar_path %>
      <%= link_to "NEXT: ON IMPULSIVITY →", bipolar_impulsivity_path %>
    </div>
  </nav>

</main>